      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Headache is one of the most common disorders that occurs during the early, developmental years of life. The present review critically discusses the most recently published reports concerning headache with onset in youngsters, delineating the current status of research in the various fields and outlining areas that require further investigation. Age-related characteristics need to be taken into account with considering the aetiology, diagnosis and treatment of juvenile headache."},
